      },
      "message": "fix(post): refuse a C-turning rapid when the machine states no C rate, with or without a C travel\n\n#906 refused a C-section rapid that turns C only when the machine\nstates a C travel but no C rate. A machine that states neither (the\nc_axis_live bench) still posted its C-turning link rapids at the max\nlinear feed scaled by the C turn - an uncapped F. The lathe post now\nrefuses that rapid by name whenever no C rate is stated.\n\nThe c_axis_live bench now states a C rate (6000/12000 deg/min, the\nshipped millturn.mch's figures) so its contour keeps posting, with every\nF checked inside the stated rates; the no-rate case is pinned on an\nunrated copy. No golden moves.\n\nFixes #966\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
